Where to look on the emulator (paths & why)

App-specific (most important)
/data/data/<package>/ or /data/user/0/<package>/ — the app's private dir.
Check subfolders:
shared_prefs/ → XMLs with config/credentials
databases/ → SQLite DBs (*.db)
files/ → saved files, config dumps
cache/ and app_webview/ → cached content
lib/ → native .so libs
no_backup/ → sometimes contains backups

APK / installed app
/data/app/<package>-*/base.apk — installed apk location (may vary)
/system/app/ and /system/priv-app/ — system APKs

External / user storage
/sdcard/ or /storage/emulated/0/ — user files, exported logs, exported configs
/sdcard/Android/data/<package>/ — app-scoped external files

Temp & misc
/data/local/tmp/ and /data/local/ — temporary files, often writable
/cache/ — system/app caches
/mnt/obb/ and /storage/ — OBB or other storage

System / config / certs
/system/etc/ — config files, sometimes embedded certs
/etc/ — config on some images
/vendor/ — vendor binaries

Native / binary inspection
/data/local/ and app lib/ for .so files to run strings / reverse

Logs / runtime
logcat (not a path) — runtime logs may leak secrets (use adb logcat)
